      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "Isocorydine, a high-transfer aporphine alkaloid, was detected in rat brain within 10 min of administration, directly demonstrating that this alkaloid class with methoxy and tertiary-amine features can cross the BBB.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "Hernandezine reached brain concentrations nearly equal to plasma Cmax after IV dosing in rats, showing extensive CNS exposure for a structurally related alkaloid.",
